  Title: Study design
  Caption: Blood samples were obtained from 42 pediatric cases of natural chikungunya ( CHIKV ) infections at an acute (d1–2) and a convalescent (d15–17) timepoint, relative to reported symptom onset. Samples were separated into whole‐blood, serum, and peripheral blood mononuclear cell ( PBMC ) aliquots for transcriptomic analysis, CHIKV viral titer assays, multiplex ELISA for cytokines, and mass cytometry (Cy TOF ). These data were combined with clinical data, including a severity score and a d15–17 anti‐ CHIKV antibody titer, to create a multiscale network of interactions during the observed course of CHIKV infection.

